# Expo SDK 54 Version Lock

Canonical mobile stack (`apps/mobile` is the only Expo app). Official SDK 54 companions ([docs](https://docs.expo.dev/versions/v54.0.0/), `bundledNativeModules.json`):

| Package | Pin |
| --- | --- |
| `expo` | `~54.0.0` (SDK **54.0.x**) |
| `react-native` | `0.81.5` (0.81.x only) |
| `react` / `react-dom` | `19.1.0` |
| `react-native-web` | `~0.21.0` |
| Expo Go | **54** (App Store latest) |

## Must

- Do not use SDK 52 or 53. Do not add packages pinned to Expo 52 (e.g. `expo-router@~4`, `react-native@0.76.x`, `react@18.3.1`).
- Do not introduce a second Expo SDK in the monorepo. Keep `apps/mobile` on 54.
- New native / Expo modules: `npx expo install <pkg>` so versions stay on the SDK 54 set. Do not add new external deps without user approval.
- Metro must resolve the Expo 54 / RN 0.81 tree. Never alias or install `react-native@0.76` as the app runtime.
- Physical iOS devices run the latest Expo Go (SDK 54). Do not tell the user to install Expo Go 52. Simulator or a matching SDK 54 dev client is fine.
- Do not run `expo upgrade` unless the user explicitly asks to upgrade the app. Until then, still never add or restore SDK 52/53 pins.

## Examples

```json
// ❌ BAD
"expo": "~52.0.0",
"react-native": "0.76.9",
"react": "18.3.1"

// ✅ GOOD
"expo": "~54.0.0",
"react-native": "0.81.5",
"react": "19.1.0"
```
